Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||07-05-2001||10:21 PM||||Ok, so it's come time to put on the side scoops I bought a while back.  I have been looking around for a rivet gun that can set monobolts, but have not had luck finding one.  I don't want to spend $175 to buy one that I will only use a time or two.  AutoZone does not have them as a loaner, and neither does the local NAPA.  Anybody know where I can get one from, or how else I might be able to set these P.I.T.A. monobolts?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||07-05-2001||10:27 PM||||Ever heard of Fastenal Company? I used to work for them here. They are all over the country. I know they have them, not sure of the cost. They used to rent tools as well. Wouldnt hurt to check them out. Or try this for a locator.<P>  <A HREF="http://www.fastenal.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastenal.com</A> <P>Hope this helps<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG">  <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"<p>[This message has been edited by V8Fiero (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||1
