Z||000004||V8Fiero||07-06-2001||11:59 PM||||That one isnt going to work. Sorry. Its only bigger to be able to set 1/4 rivets.<P>Heres another suggestion<BR>Do you have any big sign making shops in town? We used to sell a ton of mono bolts to this big outfit here and they had a pneamatic rivet gun they used. I would check with them. Maybe you could drive your car to them and it wouldnt take them very long to do it if they had the right tools.....<P>Just a suggeston<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||1
Z||000005||bad911||07-07-2001||01:40 AM||||I've been looking for a source for the big pop-rivet-type fasteners in the body and rocker panels. This is the mono bolt? I did a search on the Fastenal site and came up empty. BTW, were there OEM plastic as well as metal ones? A Pontiac parts guy did a search today and the only dealer showing them is 60 miles from me. In an old thread someone called them "pricey". Yep, 79c each.<BR>Thanks. Steve<P>------------------<BR>87 2.8 AT SE<BR>85 Caddie conv. in process<BR>84 2M4||||reg||1
